course: dictionary
lesson: 639
title: Words about swimming
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can work out many words from the words around them. «The four swimming strokes are front crawl, backstroke, breaststroke and butterfly.» The list tells you that backstroke is a kind of swimming stroke, a way of moving through the water, just like front crawl.
explain: The next clues help even more: «in front crawl the arms do most of the pushing and the legs kick mainly to keep the body flat.» Backstroke is a different stroke, so it must be done in a different way. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Backstroke can mean the whole way of swimming, or one movement of the arm in that style. When you read a word like this, look at the rest of the sentence to see which meaning the writer has chosen.
fact: Backstroke is a way of swimming on your back.
fact: In backstroke you move your arms backwards, one after the other, over your head, and you kick your legs.
fact: There are four main strokes: front crawl, backstroke, breaststroke and butterfly.
fact: Backstroke is the only race that starts in the water.
fact: In a backstroke race, swimmers see flags above the pool so they know when to turn.
exercise: «The four swimming strokes are front crawl, backstroke, breaststroke and butterfly.» How many main strokes are there? | Three | *Four | Two | Six
exercise: In backstroke, which way do the arms move? | *Backwards, one after the other, over the head | Forwards, in front of the face | Up and down by the sides | Round in circles at the sides
exercise: Which stroke is the only race that starts in the water? | Front crawl | Butterfly | Breaststroke | *Backstroke
test: What does backstroke mean? | *A way of swimming on your back, moving your arms backwards | A way of swimming on your back | A race on land | A kind of diving board
test: «There are four strokes, front crawl, backstroke, breaststroke and butterfly, and in England children are meant to swim at least 25 metres by the end of primary school.» How far should children swim by the end of primary school? | *25 metres | 100 metres | 10 metres | 50 metres
exam: Which statement about backstroke is true? | It is the stroke that never starts in the water | It is swum face down in the water | *It is swum on your back, and the arms move backwards | It has no arm movements at all
